class =\"strong\">must</span> to express something that you or a person feels is an obligation. This form is used only in the present and future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br /><span class=\"italic\">I must finish this job before I go out.<br /> Sally must explain this if she wants her students to succeed.<br /> It's late. I must get going!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Have To </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I/You/We/They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have to<br /> don't have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eat<br /> read\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He/She/It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has to <br />doesn't have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"work<br />eat\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " You use <span class =\"strong\">have/has</span>  to when it is your responsibility to do something.<br />     Have to and <span class =\"strong\">has to</span>   come before a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br />    <span class=\"italic\">You have to take warm clothes. It's cold at night.<br />    Sally has to leave home at seven o'clock every morning.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class =\"strong\">don't have to / doesn't have to</span>  when it's not necessary to do something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br />    <span class=\"italic\">It isn't cold outside. You don't have to wear a jacket.<br />    David has good boots. He doesn't have to buy a new pair.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To make a question with <span class =\"strong\">have to</span> , put <span class =\"strong\">do/does</span>   before the subject.<br />  Then add <span class =\"strong\">have to</span>   and a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Do<br /> Does</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I/ you/ we/ they<br /> he/she/it</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> have to<br /> have to </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> work on Saturdays?<br /> sleep in a tent? </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to train  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to teach (someone or something) the skills needed to do something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guides trained the dolphins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use in a personal e-mail.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reward  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of payment (to someone or something) for something good that has been done ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The dolphins got a reward for positive behavior.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "guide  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who leads or directs other people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guide took us on a tour.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fin ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thin flat part that sticks out from the body of a fish  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I held onto the dolphin's fin.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to check out  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to examine or try something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Check out my dolphin video.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pet  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gently touch an animal ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I pet the dolphin while we swam together.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le03ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a casual e-mail to a friend about a personal experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include a greeting, a question, a description, an opinion and a closing phrase.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use adjectives to make your email more interesting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Use correct punctuation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use casual language.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your e-mail aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a casual e-mail to a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe a personal experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I add description to make my writing more interesting.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "contents": [{}]}, {"title": "", "id": 2, "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le03ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": ""}, {"id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn4le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "Hey guys,<br /><br />How are you all doing? You would not believe what I did today.  I swam with three dolphins in a bay near my accommodation.  It was amazing! My guide explained that they train the dolphins with rewards like small fish. He said you must never yell around these beautiful animals, even if you get excited. If you are quiet, the dolphins come right up to you. They let you pet them and even touch their teeth! They weren't shy or nervous at all."}, {"id": 2, "time": "34000", "image": "engenn4le03ob08re2img02.jpg", "text": "The most incredible  part was when I held onto a dolphin's fin and it  carried me through the water.  We were swimming very fast together.  It was pretty cool.   I attached a video to this e-mail for you to check out.  It was great, you have to try it one day. When are you coming down here to meet me? We could have so many great adventures, like this one, together.<br />\n<br />Cheers,<br /><br />\nJohnny"}]}}], "_data": [], "type": "audio"}, {"title": "", "id": 3, "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"audiosrc": "", "coverimg": "", "images": []}}, {"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn4le03ob08re3vid01", "images": [{"id": 0, "time": "19000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">What do you include in a casual e-mail?</span>"}, {"id": 1, "time": "60000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">What kind of words do you use in e-mails?</span>"}]}}], "_data": [], "type": "video"}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can write about what people did.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write about advisab